// The AddOns domain: a seam on the client's clearing of loose interface folders.

#ifndef WXL_SEAM_GATE
#error "define WXL_SEAM_GATE(domain, name, symbol, ret, conv, params) before including addons.def"
#endif

// Moves interface folders aside on disk so that only the archives' copies load: Interface\GlueXML
// and Interface\FrameXML when they exist, and each Interface\AddOns\Blizzard* folder holding its
// .toc (DeleteInterfaceAddOns, through OsFileList), each renamed to <name>.old after an older
// .old is removed; the file hash is rebuilt when one moved. Called once by CGlueMgr::Resume, as
// the login screens start, before GlueXML.toc is judged. A free function of no argument, a bare
// `ret`: cdecl.
//
// Gated: raises InterfaceCleanupRequest; a handler that refuses it keeps the folders where they
// are, and the function does not run.
WXL_SEAM_GATE(AddOns, DeleteInterfaceFiles, "DeleteInterfaceFiles", void, cdecl, ())
WXL_SEAM_RAISES(AddOns, DeleteInterfaceFiles, InterfaceCleanupRequest)

// MSVC takes a file that expands to nothing outside its opening #ifndef X ... #endif for one
// guarded by X, and skips it when it is included again with X defined: this table is read
// several times in one translation unit, under shapes that may leave it empty. A directive
// after the rows keeps it from looking guarded.
#ifdef WXL_TABLE_END
#endif
